                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0f24dd81-d629-4965-bdd1-ff52c1d44fee",
                        "entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "génépis"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "63544e4f-dc6f-4674-85bb-0184a76cf79f",
                        "entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "génipi"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec3b900a-5054-33c5-a6cf-b4c5172a1728",
                        "entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom vernaculaire de plusieurs espèces de plantes du genre Artemisia, dont certaines sont utilisées comme plantes médicinales ou pour la fabrication de boissons alcoolisées."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ab7c069-e424-48e0-b261-68f8c895b1d2",
                                "sense_id": "ec3b900a-5054-33c5-a6cf-b4c5172a1728",
                                "text": "Dans une course qu’Anet avait fait au haut des montagnes pour aller chercher du génépi, plante rare qui ne croît que sur les Alpes, et dont M. Grossi avait besoin, ce pauvre garçon s’échauffa tellement qu’il gagna une pleurésie dont le génépi ne put le sauver, quoiqu’il y soit, dit-on, spécifique ; …"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00bff761-4fe0-3654-8686-d6ae565fd875",
                        "entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Liqueur obtenue par macération alcoolique du génépi."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d44e193-6092-4ed0-8540-c770fd555d24",
                                "sense_id": "00bff761-4fe0-3654-8686-d6ae565fd875",
                                "text": "En digestif, on proposa du génépi et de la gentiane."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1b267458-ba33-471b-8944-8cc347a4152f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "target_lang_word": "wormwood",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wormwood",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                        "entry_id": "64d298af-fcfd-3e70-9a42-9b3e8100189d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intensely bitter herb (Artemisia absinthium and similar plants in genus Artemisia) used in medicine, in the production of absinthe and vermouth, and as a tonic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b45e8bcd-2a35-4862-9377-b91b8cc9ed7e",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "But as I said, / When it did taste the wormwood on the nipple / Of my dug and felt it bitter, pretty fool, / To see it tetchy and fall out with the dug!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35b189b2-2e0a-47bb-a97e-3b2e0c99c5b0",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will feed them, even this people, with wormwood, and give them water of gall to drink."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28b2ddd4-3520-4f56-93ec-a75b750ce509",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "Blue skippers in sunny hours ope and shut\nWhere wormwood and grunsel flowers by the cart ruts […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f51eb0f2-2c43-400d-ac72-50a1225a2c74",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "Cliff took two glasses and filled one with wine\nAnd one with wormwood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13a44e72-31ed-44b3-871f-1437bde7caf8",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "Amongst the herbs to be administered when the charm was sung over him were a yew-berry, lupin, helenium, marsh mallow, dock, elder, wormwood and strawberry leaves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96c87a38-7de6-4c5e-86ea-8f8bf3a760bc",
                                                "sense_id": "71e35fcc-2b0e-308a-a9d3-9af6c9cf4d56",
                                                "text": "Tradition credits John the Baptist with wearing a girdle fashioned of wormwood, while he was in the wilderness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff660978-1408-3bb7-a54e-cd4b926e4375",
                                        "entry_id": "64d298af-fcfd-3e70-9a42-9b3e8100189d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that causes bitterness or affliction; a cause of mortification or vexation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f613c597-aff6-45e4-b175-2784d5abab83",
                                                "sense_id": "ff660978-1408-3bb7-a54e-cd4b926e4375",
                                                "text": "The irony of this reply was wormwood to Zeluco; he fell into a gloomy fit of musing, and made no farther inquiry […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "971968ea-73cb-426a-a30e-a856f65f74cf",
                                                "sense_id": "ff660978-1408-3bb7-a54e-cd4b926e4375",
                                                "text": "Yet I think the Archdeacon, a \"new man,\" to whom the aristocratic Canon's popularity was wormwood, did dislike him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf2e57e9-54be-43ad-a75c-4445f16f7ef3",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3eeba8f-6189-315b-b82b-deeeb85f865d",
                        "target_lang_word": "artemisia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "artemisia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "206029ee-ec18-3c76-89ad-9fec430b073f",
                                        "entry_id": "0520e3e6-2830-3f15-87fc-ac73365b22e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of many aromatic flowering plants of the genus Artemisia, including wormwood, sagebrush, and tarragon, often used as traditional medicine, oral contraceptive and flavoring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2afdfa6-cfbf-44a4-84b3-a464e692f998",
                                                "sense_id": "206029ee-ec18-3c76-89ad-9fec430b073f",
                                                "text": "In the event of anyone wishing to invoke the very Prince of Spirits, the following ingredients were prescribed to be burnt - Juice of Hypericon, Saffron, Artemisia, and the root of Valerian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b0c4176-1c90-406a-a2f9-28e7ccffdda1",
                                                "sense_id": "206029ee-ec18-3c76-89ad-9fec430b073f",
                                                "text": "Our central issue, however, is whether the artemisia of Dioscorides is mugwort. Fuchs in Germany shows no hesitation in accepting the beyfusz of his country, called armoise by the French and Artemisia latifolia or broadleaved artemisia by the Italians, is the artemisia of Dioscorides, Galen, and Pliny, and he quotes them exactly on the plant's medicinal actions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
